1. श्रम् cl. 4. P. (Dhātup. xxvi, 95) श्राम्यति (in later language also श्रमति, ते; pf. शश्रम, 3. pl. शश्रमुः or [ŚāṅkhBr.] श्रेमुः, p. शश्रमाण॑, RV.; MBh.; aor. अ॑श्रमत्, AV., Subj. श्रमत्, RV.; श्रमिष्म, ib.; Br.; fut. श्रमिता, MBh.; श्रमिष्यति Gr.; inf. श्रमितुम्, ib.; ind.p. -श्र॑म्य, Br.),
to be or become weary or tired, be tired of doing anything (with inf.; also impers. न॑ मा श्रमत्, ‘may I not become weary!’), RV. &c. &c.;
to make effort, exert one's self (esp. in performing acts of austerity), labour in vain, ib. :
Pass. श्रम्यते (aor. अश्रामि or अश्रमि, Gr.), MBh.; Kāv. &c. (cf. वि-√ श्रं) :
Caus. श्रामयति or श्रमयति (aor. अशिश्रमत्), to make weary, fatigue, tire, Kām.; Hariv.; Subh.;
to overcome, conquer, subdue, R.;
 (श्रामयति), to speak to, address, invite (आमन्त्रणे), Dhātup. xxxv, 40 (v.l. for ग्राम्˚, cf. ग्रामय) :
Desid. See वि-शिश्रमिषु.

